{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T21:58:53.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ddb2e572b3dc24915ab9fe76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-03q389","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-5kfzjh"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Managed npm update checks report a subprocess timeout as npm_registry_lookup_failed, and the fixed 10 s npm view budget makes the Windows nightly extension-freshness test flaky"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Nightly run 44087418672 (GitHub alert issue 1747, windows-latest Node 24 shard 4/4) failed tests/integration/extensions/extension-diagnostic-purity.integration.spec.ts in both the initial attempt and the retry (21.6 s for two attempts) at its first registry-backed freshness check: update_check_status was failed instead of checked. The test passes in 5.3 s on green Windows nights (run 43867277935) while spawning npm view several times, so each failing attempt spent the full GITHUB_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS (10 s) on one cold npm view through the Windows command shell. runNpmUpdateQuery in src/sdk/extension/update-check.ts maps every failure, including that timeout, to the stable code npm_registry_lookup_failed, so neither the nightly log nor a user's pm extension --manage output can tell a slow npm from an unavailable registry. Proposed: report a distinct stable code for a timed-out lookup (killed subprocess with ETIMEDOUT or SIGTERM) without echoing npm's command, stderr or environment, name the budget in the diagnostic, and give the integration test a deterministic registry check budget so Windows cold npm starts do not fail it. Related evidence work: pm-q7c36n kept subprocess timeout and signal evidence for registry install acceptance; pm-2zjs0g measures nightly family rates."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["diagnostics","extensions","flaky-test","gh:1747","nightly","update-check","windows"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:53.463Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:53.463Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A timed-out npm update lookup reports a distinct stable code (no npm command, stderr or environment in the output) and the diagnostic names the budget; the extension-diagnostic-purity integration test no longer depends on a cold Windows npm start finishing inside 10 s; unit tests cover the timeout and failure classifications"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A slow npm view is reported as a timeout distinct from an unavailable registry, and the Windows nightly freshness test is deterministic"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Every lookup failure, including the 10 s timeout, is npm_registry_lookup_failed, and the Windows nightly test failed twice at the timeout"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"extensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-2zjs0g","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T21:58:53.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-q7c36n","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T21:58:53.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ab15c9905ab52a0ec28726ff65cd114be016b8ff7da9008d5836fe63eaaedcba","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2834fcc346aea1ce007d1b205513e2ddb5589c6a67e821dc6ecf9a8c2df52688"}
